{"id":"tola","name":"Tola","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:tola"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Tola","text":"A scarlet worm. (1.) Eldest son of Issachar (Gen. 46:13). (2.) A judge of the tribe of Issachar who “judged” Israel twenty-three years (Judg. 10:1, 2), when he died, and was buried in Shamir. He was succeeded by Jair."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H8439","lemma":"תּוֹלָע","xlit":"Tôwlâʻ","gloss":"Tola, the name of two Israelites","kjv":"Tola","count":5,"share":0.83},{"strong":"H6312","lemma":"פּוּאָה","xlit":"Pûwʼâh","gloss":"Puah or Puvvah, the name of two Israelites","kjv":"Phuvah, Pua, Puah","count":4,"share":0.67},{"strong":"H3485","lemma":"יִשָּׂשכָר","xlit":"Yissâˢkâr","gloss":"Jissaskar, a son of Jacob","kjv":"Issachar","count":4,"share":0.67},{"strong":"H8069","lemma":"שָׁמִיר","xlit":"Shâmîyr","gloss":"Shamir, the name of two places in Palestine","kjv":"Shamir","count":2,"share":0.33},{"strong":"H8110","lemma":"שִׁמְרוֹן","xlit":"Shimrôwn","gloss":"Shimron, the name of an Israelite and of a place in Pale","kjv":"Shimron","count":2,"share":0.33},{"strong":"H6242","lemma":"עֶשְׂרִים","xlit":"ʻesrîym","gloss":"twenty","kjv":"score, twenty","count":2,"share":0.33}],"verses":["Gen.46.13","Num.26.23","Judg.10.1","1Chr.7.1","1Chr.7.2","Judg.10.2"],"related":[{"id":"phuvah","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.5,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"issachar-the-tribe-of","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.068,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"phuvah","type":"lexical","strong":"H8439","why":"both lead with תּוֹלָע (H8439)"}],"works":[{"work":"anf02","title":"Ante-Nicene Fathers, Volume 2: Fathers of the Second Century","count":1,"chapters":[{"chapter":"ANFXI.1","count":1,"book":"The Stromata, or Miscellanie","title":"Book I"}]}]}
